==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|goh|loup}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*laubą}}, perhaps from {{der|de|ine-pro|*lewp-||peel, break off}}. Compare {{cog|nds|Loov}}, {{cog|nl|loof}}, {{cog|en|leaf}}, {{cog|da|løv}}. The Indo-European root is *leup- which is (presumably by oversight) omitted from the online [https://www.ahdictionary.com/word/indoeurop.html American Heritage Dictionary of Indo-European Roots] but included in the [https://www.hmhco.com/shop/books/The-American-Heritage-Dictionary-of-IndoEuropean-Roots-Third-Edition/9780547549446 book version].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/laʊ̯p/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Laub.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|aʊ̯p|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n|Laubes|gen2=Laubs|-}}

# {{lb|de|collective}} [[foliage]], [[greenery]], [[leaves]] {{gloss|on a tree or fallen onto the ground, but particularly the latter}}
#: {{uxi|de|grünes '''Laub'''}}
#: {{uxi|de|fallendes '''Laub'''}}
#* Hans Wollschläger, ''Von Sternen und Schnuppen: bei Gelegenheit einiger Bücher'', volume 1, page 209:
#*: {{quote|de|Sie [die Orangen] hängen eben tatsächlich mitten im grünen '''Laub''' gelb an den Bäumen.}}

